//====================================================
// ESP32 GAME STATION
// LINEAR SESSION MEMORY ARENA CONTRACT
// 131_memory_arena.h
//====================================================
//
// Responsibilities:
// - Reserves one contiguous backing block from MemoryManager.
// - Serves aligned sub-allocations without repeated malloc/free calls.
// - Supports markers, rewind and constant-time full reset.
// - Tracks current, remaining and peak memory usage per arena.
// - Keeps internal-RAM and PSRAM placement explicit.
// - Prevents stale markers from rewinding a restarted arena.
//
// Lifetime rule:
// - Memory returned by allocate() remains valid until rewind(), reset(),
//   end() or destruction of the arena.
// - The arena does not run constructors or destructors for objects stored
//   inside it. Callers must manage non-trivial object lifetimes manually.
// - Individual allocations cannot be released out of order.
//
// Integration rule:
// - File 132 implements this contract using MemoryManager.
// - ResourceBudgetCoordinator will create arenas only after admission.
// - PDF, audio, emulator and game sessions may own separate arenas.
// - DMA buffers must continue to use internal DMA-capable allocation and
//   must not be placed in a PSRAM-backed arena.
//====================================================

