//====================================================
// ESP32 GAME STATION
// BOUNDED SD FILE STREAMING SERVICE CONTRACT
// 137_sd_stream_service.h
//====================================================
//
// Responsibilities:
// - Keeps a bounded number of SD files open for streaming clients.
// - Prefetches file data into StreamRingBuffer instances.
// - Supports non-blocking read, peek, skip and seek operations.
// - Shares one per-update byte budget fairly between active streams.
// - Retries temporary SD read failures without blocking the frame loop.
// - Rejects stale handles through slot generations.
// - Reports source offsets, buffered bytes, EOF and retry diagnostics.
//
// Ownership rule:
// - Arduino File objects remain private to file 138.
// - Callers interact only through SdStreamHandle values.
// - A handle becomes invalid immediately after close(), closeAll() or end().
//
// Buffer rule:
// - Compressed files and large assets normally use PSRAM-backed buffers.
// - DMA output buffers must remain in internal DMA-capable memory.
// - Seeking clears prefetched data before loading from the new position.
//
// Integration rule:
// - File 138 implements this contract using SD, StorageManager and
//   StreamRingBuffer.
// - Audio, PDF, emulator and asset systems may share this service.
// - update() should be called once per main-loop iteration.
//====================================================

