// ESP32-S3 I2S AUDIO OUTPUT BACKEND CONTRACT
// 141_i2s_audio_backend.h
//====================================================
//
// Responsibilities:
// - Owns the ESP32-S3 transmit-only I2S peripheral lifecycle.
// - Sends signed 16-bit PCM frames to MAX98357A / PCM5102A hardware.
// - Keeps every DMA descriptor and sample buffer in internal RAM.
// - Supports bounded blocking or non-blocking frame submission.
// - Applies speaker, headphone and muted routing through optional amp pins.
// - Allows safe sample-rate/channel reconfiguration between streams.
// - Reports partial writes, timeouts, underruns and driver failures.
//
// Data rule:
// - write() accepts interleaved signed 16-bit PCM frames.
// - One frame contains channelCount samples.
// - Mono input may be duplicated by the backend when configured.
// - Caller-owned sample memory must remain valid until write() returns.
//
// Memory rule:
// - DMA-capable memory must never be allocated from PSRAM.
// - begin() reserves the estimated internal-RAM requirement through
//   ResourceBudgetCoordinator before installing the hardware driver.
// - Driver resources and the matching budget are released by end().
//
// Routing rule:
// - MAX98357A and PCM5102A may share BCLK, WS and DATA_OUT.
// - Optional amplifier-enable pins select the audible physical route.
// - When enable pins are not connected, AudioRoute remains a logical
//   policy value and Muted still prevents PCM submission.
//
// Integration rule:
// - File 142 implements this contract using the supported Arduino-ESP32
//   I2S API without exposing version-specific driver types here.
// - File 151 bridges legacy AudioOutput to this backend.
// - PCM ring buffer and stream engine feed this backend in later files.
//====================================================

