//====================================================
// ESP32 GAME STATION
// SINGLE-PRODUCER / SINGLE-CONSUMER PCM RING BUFFER
// 143_pcm_ring_buffer.h
//====================================================
//
// Responsibilities:
// - Stores interleaved signed 16-bit PCM as complete audio frames.
// - Preserves frame boundaries across every copy and zero-copy operation.
// - Supports one producer and one consumer running on separate tasks/cores.
// - Provides bounded underrun handling with optional silence padding.
// - Rejects or overwrites old frames according to an explicit policy.
// - Tracks high-water, low-water, underrun, overflow and latency metrics.
// - Owns MemoryManager storage or attaches to caller-owned sample memory.
//
// Concurrency rule:
// - Exactly one producer may call write-side functions.
// - Exactly one consumer may call read-side functions.
// - Producer and consumer may run concurrently.
// - Lifecycle, reset, format and policy functions require both sides stopped.
// - Observer callbacks execute in the calling context and must not re-enter.
//
// Audio rule:
// - One frame contains channelCount signed 16-bit samples.
// - Sample rate is metadata used for duration/latency calculations.
// - The buffer never resamples, mixes or changes channel layout.
// - Format conversion belongs to AudioStreamEngine or decoder adapters.
//
// Memory rule:
// - Long PCM staging buffers normally use PSRAM.
// - I2S DMA memory remains owned by I2sAudioBackend in internal RAM.
// - External storage must be aligned for int16_t and outlive this object.
//
// Integration rule:
// - File 144 implements this contract.
// - WAV/MP3 decoders write frames through producer operations.
// - AudioStreamEngine consumes frames and submits them to file 141/142.
//====================================================

namespace egs
{
